1
00:04:54,285 --> 00:05:00,285
In nature, there are boundaries. One man spent the last
thirteen years of his life crossing them.

2
00:09:48,571 --> 00:09:54,571
Grizzly Man is a documentary film directed by Werner Herzog.

3
00:14:42,857 --> 00:14:48,857
Follows the story of "Grizzly Man" Timothy Treadwell and what the thirteen summers in a
National Park in Alaska were like in his attempt to protect the grizzly bears.

4
00:19:37,142 --> 00:19:43,142
The film is full of unique images and a look into the spirit
of a man who sacrificed himself for nature.

5
00:24:31,428 --> 00:24:37,428
Self - Actor, Close Friend, played by Warren Queeney.

6
00:29:25,714 --> 00:29:31,714
Self - Pilot, Former Rodeo Rider, played by Willy Fulton.

7
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:26,000
Self - Egli Air Haul, played by Sam Egli.

8
00:39:14,285 --> 00:39:20,285
Self - Ecologist, played by Marnie Gaede.

9
00:44:08,571 --> 00:44:14,571
Self - Ecologist, played by Marc Gaede.

10
00:49:02,857 --> 00:49:08,857
Self - Bear Biologist, played by Larry Van Daele.

11
00:53:57,142 --> 00:54:03,142
Grizzly Man is a 2005 American documentary film
written and directed by Werner Herzog.

12
00:58:51,428 --> 00:58:57,428
It chronicles the life and death of bear enthusiast and conservationist Timothy
Treadwell and his girlfriend Amie Huguenard at Katmai National Park, Alaska.

13
01:03:45,714 --> 01:03:51,714
The film includes some of Treadwell's own footage of his interactions with brown bears before 2003, and of interviews with
people who knew or were involved with Treadwell, in addition to professionals who deal with wild bears.

14
01:08:40,000 --> 01:08:46,000
Treadwell and Huguenard, both from New York, had bonded over their common passion for bears and
animal conservation, and she would occasionally accompany him on his trips to the park.

15
01:13:34,285 --> 01:13:40,285
Having stayed past the summer season one year, the pair were attacked
and killed in the park by a bear on October 5, 2003.

16
01:18:28,571 --> 01:18:34,571
The couple's remains were discovered by a patrolling pilot, and an audio recording of the attack was found
among the remains; the bear was later tracked down and killed by the pilot's rescue team.

17
01:23:22,857 --> 01:23:28,857
The film was co-produced by Discovery Docs and Lions Gate Entertainment.

18
01:28:17,142 --> 01:28:23,142
The film's soundtrack was composed by Richard Thompson.

19
01:33:11,428 --> 01:33:17,428
It received widespread acclaim from critics and is now considered to be
among the best films of the 2000s and of the 21st century.

20
01:38:05,714 --> 01:38:11,714
The film explores themes of self-abandonment, life and death,
unsociability, grizzly bear, human animal relationship.
